{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>The daughter of the ostrich.</b> Therefore it uses 'daughter' because it is fit only when it is small, for its flesh is hard as wood when it is large." "<b>And the nes.</b> This too is not the bird we call ashperbir, for it has three signs of purity, as is concluded in the chapter אלו טרפות — תלתא הדרי בכולהו, and the Tosafot there prove that the sign that is only in the peres or in the aznayah is a peelable crop, and if so, the three signs of purity that the nes has are: an extra toe and it is not a bird of prey. But the ashperuir we see every day that it is a bird of prey — both according to Rashi, who explains that it seizes its food with its feet, and according to Rabbenu Tam, who explained that 'bird of prey' means it eats the bird alive."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:59.237719828Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}